[[512,16,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic injection system.</p><p>The supply for the engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\ncontrolled by the ignition (15/54) at pin 58 by the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the  system\nsupply: it is supplied by the battery, from the line for maxifuse\nEFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; pin 13 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends the\nenablement signal which excites relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends power\nto the control unit, directly to pin 5 and, fia the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F3</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , to pin 4.</p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is also supplied by\nthe battery, from the  line for maxifuse EFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; pin\n24 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends the signals which energize the\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which provides the supply to the fuel pump \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhich is connected to earth through the inertia switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nIn case of impact, this cuts off the circuit to prevent the danger\nof fuel delivery.</p><p>Pins 1, 2 and 3 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               are earthed.</p><p>The diesel preheating relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nsupplied by the battery via th eline protected by the GLOW maxifuse\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B39</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , and controls the operation of\nthe diesel heating resistor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; a signal of the control\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (from pin 111) deactivates the system once heating\nhas taken place.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , responsible for\ncontrolling preheating of heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , is supplied directly\nby the battery via a line protected by the GLOW maxifuse of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nIt is supplied - connector C - by the line of fuse F2 of the additional fuse\nbox \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , and exchanges the command and control signals with\npins 22 and 62 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which controls the time lag. Connector\nB is connected to the heater plugs \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A40.</strong></p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\nservice conditions.</p><p>The rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\nconcerning the engine speed through a frequency signal sent to pin\n100 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives an earth signal\nfrom pin 99 of the control unit. Both signals are weak and are therefore suitably\nshielded by pin 101.</p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\npin 102 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a reference earth\nfrom pin 104 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends it a frequency signal\ncorresponding to the timing to pin 103.</p><p>The engine temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nreceives a reference earth from pin 85 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to the temperature of the engine\ncoolant to pin 84.</p><p>The same sender unit also supplies information\nto the temperature gauge and warning light \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a\ngeneral power supply from the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; it receives a reference voltage from pin 88 of \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It is supplied by the control unit from pin 97 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nand sends to pin 89 a signal proportional to the air flow. \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also\ncontains an air temperature sensor which sends an air temperature\nsignal to pin 86 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Accelerator pedal \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K55</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              is fitted with\ntwo built-in potentiometers (a main one and a safety back-up). The\nfirst receives power and earth from pins 78 and 76 respectively\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a corresponding signal to pin 77. The second receives\npower and earth from pins 81 and 79 respectively of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsends a signal to pin 80.</p><p>Fuel temperature sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K81</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               fitted\non the return manifold measures the temperature of diesel leaving\nthe injectors. It receives a reference earth from pin 83 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsends a fuel temperature signal to control unit pin 82.</p><p>The turbocharging sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K82</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               records\nturbo pressure. It is supplied by pin 93 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and receives\na reference earth from pin 95. The signal is sent to pin 94 of the\ncontrol unit.</p><p>The fuel pressure sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K83</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is responsible\nfor providing the injection control unit with a feedback signal\nfor governing pressure and injection duration. It receives the power\nand reference earth from pins 90 and 92 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; it then sends\nthe pressure signal to pin 91.</p><p>The fuel pressure regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N77</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has\nthe task of keeping the value of the fuel pressure in the accumulator\nconstant. The two control signals come from pins 108 and 109 of\nthe control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The EGR solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls exhaust\ngas recirculation. It is supplied from the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and is controlled by a signal of\npin 16 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The turbine variable geometry control solenoid \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               governs the operation of the turbine in accordance with\nengine load; it is supplied by the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the\nadditional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and is controlled by a signal from\npin 17 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The solenoid on the throttle body \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L62</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               chokes\nand closes the butterfly, for example when the engine is turned\noff; it is supplied by the line of fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and is controlled by a signal of pin 15 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 59 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives the signal\ncoming from the brake lights switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , with the supply\ncontrolled by the ignition (INT) from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the junction\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong><a href=\"#/3233830\">E2021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 62 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives an earth signal\ncoming from the clutch pedal switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>l31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive a power\nsupply to enable opening from pins 117 and 118 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The engine management control unit sends\ncommands to the injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from pins 119, 120, 121, 114\nand 115 respectively for cylinders 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5.</p><p>The rev counter module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; when the earth\nsignal arrives from pin 21 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , the &#x27;injection failure&#x27;\nwarning light comes on.</p><p>The speedometer module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; when the earth\nsignal arrives from pin 14 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , the &#x27;heater plugs&#x27; warning\nlight comes on.</p><p>The coolant temperature signal is sent to\nthe auxiliary instrument from pin 110 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong><a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected\nto the ALFA ROMEO CODE control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via a specific line\nfrom pin 11; in this way if the ALFA ROMEO CODE unit does not detect\na correct code, it does not issue enablement and the engine is not\nstarted.</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nunit that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via\npin 48.</p><p>The speedometer signal (vehicle speed) reaches\npin 49 of control unit  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong><a href=\"#/3234310\">E4021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends a signal\nfrom pin 47 proportional to the engine speed \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected\nto the air conditioning system through pins 18 and 60. This makes\nit possible to adjust the engine idle speed as the load increases\neach time the compressor is switched on or to switch off the compressor\nin the case of high engine speed or load conditions \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pins 19, 20, 51 and 52 control the engagement of\nthe relevant fans \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"]]